SUMMARY: Art and Film/Film as Art at The Kimbell Cultural Event Center
DESCRIPTION:\nThe Queen’s Film Society and the Program in Performance and
  Visual Studies at Texas A&M University Present:\n\nArt & Film/Film as Ar
 t\n\nStep into a world where cinema and canvas collide. The art exhibitio
 n “Art and Film/Film as Art”\, opening Friday\, August 28 and continuing 
 through September at the Kimbell Cultural Event Center\, brings together 
 bold new work by artists including F. C. Zuke\, Beast Syndicate\, Lauren 
 Cardenas\, Joel Zika\, who explore the thrilling back-and-forth dialogues
  between iconic films and visual art. The exhibition is paired with a fil
 m series showcasing acclaimed motion pictures from around the world that\
 , in their cinematography and aesthetic design\, similarly reflect the im
 pact of fine and illustrative art. The film selection spans from the 1940
 s to the 2020s\, and each screening will be preceded by a formal introduc
 tion by a cinema or art history scholar. The film series will also be acc
 ompanied by a comparative installation showing how art images and their f
 ilmic recreations in these films and others represent a dialog between di
 fferent artists across centuries and media. Finally\, in addition to the 
 August 28 opening reception at the Kimbell\, there will be a closing rece
 ption on September 24 as well as artist talks\, scholarly lectures\, and 
 public presentations by artists and scholars throughout the month.\n\n\nR
 eceptions with Artists’ Talks:\n\nThe Kimbell Cultural Event Center\, 607
  North Main Street\, Bryan\, TX\, 77803\n\n  * Opening Reception: Friday\
 , August 28: 6-10 pm.\n  * Closing Reception: Thursday\, September 24: 6-
 9 pm.\n\n\nGallery Exhibition Hours:\n\nAug. 28-Sept. 29\n\nThe Kimbell C
 ultural Event Center\, 607 North Main Street\, Bryan\, TX\, 77803\n\n  * 
 Tuesdays: 6-10 pm\n  * Wednesdays: 2-4 pm\n  * Fridays: 2-10 pm\n  * Satu
 rdays: 2-6 pm\n\nNote: Like most exhibitions involving classic and contem
 porary art\, Art & Film/Film as Art contains images featuring nudity\, vi
 olence\, and other potentially disturbing subject matter.\n\nAdmission to
  the exhibition is free and unticketed.\n\n\nFilm Series:\n\nThe Wings of
  the Dove (Iain Softley\, UK 1997\, 102 min.)\, The Queen Theatre\, 7pm\,
  Sept 1. Rated R. Free for Queen's Film Society Members\; $10 for the gen
 eral public.\n\nWild Strawberries (Ingmar Bergman\, Sweden 1957\, 92 min.
 )\, The Kimbell\, 7pm\, Sept 8. Not Rated\, likely PG. Free for Queen's F
 ilm Society Members\; $7 for the general public.\n\nPan’s Labyrinth (Guil
 lermo del Toro\, Mexico/Spain 2006\, 118 min.)\, The Kimbell\, 7pm\, Sept
  15. Rated R. Free for Queen's Film Society Members\; $7 for the general 
 public.\n\nMamma Roma (Pier Paolo Pasolini\, Italy 1962\, 110 min.)\, The
  Kimbell\, 7pm\, Sept 22. Not Rated\, likely PG-13. Free for Queen's Film
  Society Members\; $7 for the general public.\n\nLiquid Sky (Slava Tsuker
 man\, US 1982\, 112 min.)\, The 101\, 8pm\, Sept 24. Rated R. Free and un
 -ticketed.\n\nBedlam (Mark Robson\, US 1946\, 79 min.)\, The Kimbell\, 7p
 m\, Sept 29. Not Rated\, likely PG. Free for Queen's Film Society Members
 \; $7 for the general public.\n\nSinners (Ryan Coogler\, US 2025\, 137 mi
 n.)\, The Queen Theatre\, 7pm\, Sept 30. Rated R. Free tickets for this s
 creening will be available for this screening via the College of Performa
 nce\, Visualization & Fine Arts. Contact Dan Humphrey at: danhumphrey@tam
 u.edu mailto:danhumphrey@tamu.edu .\n\nTickets available at: http://thequ
 eensfilmsociety.org.
CATEGORIES:
