SUMMARY: BVCA November Swiss - Chess Tournament
DESCRIPTION:Monthly USCF-Rated Chess Tournaments - All Ages & Skill Level
 s Welcome!\n\n\nThe Brazos Valley Chess Association hosts USCF-rated ches
 s tournaments one Saturday every month at First Baptist Church Bryan (9:3
 0 AM - 4:30 PM). Whether you're a seasoned veteran or just a beginner\, o
 ur tournaments offer an excellent opportunity to test your skills and con
 nect with the local chess community!\nWhat to Expect:\n\n  * Official USC
 F rating opportunities - grow your official rating\n  * Professional tour
 nament format with a professional attitude\n  * Multiple sections based o
 n skill level - compete with similar players to you!\n  * Welcoming\, sup
 portive atmosphere for players of all ages\n  * Great for homeschoolers\,
  after-schoolers\, and weekend warriors\n  * Great learning activity and 
 character builder for students\n  * Connect with fellow chess enthusiasts
  across the BCS area\n\nWhy Chess Tournaments?\nChess develops critical t
 hinking\, strategic planning\, problem-solving skills\, and sportsmanship
 . Tournament play takes these benefits to the next level by teaching play
 ers to perform under pressure and think creatively in competitive situati
 ons.\n\nTournament Schedule:\nThe full 2026 calendar is posted at http://
 BrazosValleyChess.com http://brazosvalleychess.com BrazosValleyChess.com 
 - plan out your chess experience today!\n\n\nLocation: First Baptist Brya
 n\n3100 Cambridge Dr.\nBryan\, TX 77802\n(979) 776-1400\n\n\nRegistration
 : NOW OPEN at http://BrazosValleyChess.com http://brazosvalleychess.com B
 razosValleyChess.com\n\n\nPerfect for families looking for enriching week
 end activities\, students building competitive experience\, or anyone who
  loves the timeless game of chess. We hope you will join us on your chess
  journey!
CATEGORIES:chess,chess-tournament,USCF,educational
