SUMMARY: The Dolly Show
DESCRIPTION:Blinn's 2026-27 Performing Arts Series concludes with rhinest
 ones\, powerhouse vocals\, comedy\, and country music as “The Dolly Show”
  brings the spirit\, sound\, and sparkle of Dolly Parton to the O’Donnell
  Center stage.\n\nBacked by a live band\, the theatrical concert takes au
 diences on a journey through six decades of Parton’s greatest songs. The 
 production combines dazzling costumes\, storytelling\, humor\, and audien
 ce interaction in a celebration of one of music’s most beloved entertaine
 rs.\n\nAt the heart of the production is Australian-born performer Kelly 
 O’Brien\, who has entertained professionally for more than 25 years. O’Br
 ien began singing country music at age 14 and\, two years later\, was nam
 ed South Australian Country Vocalist of the Year and Best New Talent at t
 he Gympie Music Muster\, leading to her first recording contract.\n\nO’Br
 ien has been endorsed by members of the Parton family and selected by Dol
 ly Parton Enterprises to serve as Parton’s body double for film. Her voic
 e\, mannerisms\, warmth\, and stage presence have made her one of the wor
 ld’s most acclaimed Dolly Parton performers.\n\n“Wow! Kelly is fierce as 
 Dolly\,” singer Michael Bublé said.\n\nThe show will feature Parton favor
 ites including “Jolene\,” “9 to 5\,” “Islands in the Stream\,” “Coat of M
 any Colors\,” and “I Will Always Love You.” Parton’s original recording o
 f “I Will Always Love You” twice reached No. 1 on the country charts befo
 re Whitney Houston introduced the song to a new generation through the fi
 lm “The Bodyguard.”\n\nTickets are available at www.blinn.edu/boxoffice h
 ttps://nam04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.blinn
 .edu%2Fboxoffice&data=05%7C02%7Crichard.bray%40blinn.edu%7C52cebcd0e5ce43
 8884e608def6eaf844%7C60448a85d0074d57a583bfec98e99c29%7C1%7C0%7C639219686
 257480628%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJFbXB0eU1hcGkiOnRydWUsIlYiOiIwLjAuMDA
 wMCIsIlAiOiJXaW4zMiIsIkFOIjoiTWFpbCIsIldUIjoyfQ%3D%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&sdata=
 N9%2FJzjWKUosC2puJ2Z6MlsAj7h6SV%2FJw6%2F%2F5%2FryjsqE%3D&reserved=0 or by
  calling 979-830-4024.
CATEGORIES:music,live-music,performing-arts
